          "content": {
            "mimeType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
            "text": "\r\n\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<!--[if lt IE 7]> \t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie6 lte9 lte8 lte7 \">\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 7]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie7 lte9 lte8 lte7 \">\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 8]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie8 lte9 lte8 \">\t\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 9]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie9 lte9 \">\t\t\t\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if (gt IE 9)|!(IE)]><!-->\r\n<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\r\n<!--<![endif]-->\r\n<head id=\"Head1\"><title>\r\n\tProgrammers of Tomorrow fundraiser screening #1: Goodbye, Dragon Inn (2003) Tickets | 05 Sep @ The Cinema Museum, London | £9 to £12 | OutSavvy\r\n</title>\r\n\r\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n        window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];\r\n\r\n        function gtag() { dataLayer.push(arguments); }\r\n\r\n        if (window.location.hash ? window.location.hash == '#cs-scan' : false) {\r\n            gtag(\"consent\", \"default\", { ad_storage: \"granted\", ad_user_data: \"granted\", ad_personalization: \"granted\", analytics_storage: \"granted\", functionality_storage: \"granted\", personalization_storage: \"granted\", security_storage: \"granted\", wait_for_update: 500 });\r\n        }\r\n        else {\r\n            gtag(\"consent\", \"default\", {\r\n                ad_storage: \"denied\",\r\n                ad_user_data: \"denied\",\r\n                ad_personalization: \"denied\",\r\n                analytics_storage: \"denied\",\r\n                functionality_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                personalization_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                security_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                wait_for_update: 500,\r\n            });\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        gtag(\"set\", \"ads_data_redaction\", true);\r\n\r\n        gtag(\"set\", \"developer_id.dZTlmZj\", true);\r\n    </script>\r\n\r\n    <script async src=\"https://consent.studio/outsavvy.com/banner.js\"></script>\r\n\r\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/combres.axd/siteCss/7fe0f610674626944167a99dcfa57a351cfe742a930afe976c016bb3f608223c5956cdd8ab3167f15d9b50a337b27eba0ccb8113b99bd5e19f1cee33041b1821/\"/><script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/combres.axd/siteJs/4ea27d3d3dfdcea6aa2256650964498a5d720acb896b38d1bcbc2a81e57470911dd600418c7f575901cd7b3741c1b3a433126ce5ab0a56f134539cecb5333ade/\"></script>\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"Priority\" content=\"1.0\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"ChangeFrequency\" content=\"daily\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta http-equiv=\"last-modified\" name=\"LastModified\" content=\"2026-08-31\" />\r\n\r\n    \r\n    <meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow\" />\r\n    \r\n\r\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"‘Did you know this theatre is haunted?’The Cinema of Tomorrow (F.K.A PEPCOT) presents the first of three screenings on the theme of ‘Movies at the Movies’. Goodbye, Dragon Inn (2003) is a beautiful, melancholic and quietly funny exploration of intimacy and isolation over the course of the last day at a closing picture palace in Taipei City, Taiwan. Director Tsai Ming-Liang, master of the slow and closely observed, mourns the loss of some of the sacred rituals of cinema going, from cruising to shelling peanuts in the dark.This is the first event (and therefore launch. ) of Programmers of Tomorrow (PoT): A season of workshops and screenings for the future of film exhibition. Consisting of two free workshops, three fundraiser screenings and a film festival all-dayer, PoT will spread knowledge about film programming, build community around the love of movies, and facilitate first timers to put on their first ever public screening.  Read more about it and how to get involved.This screening is a fundraiser for both PoT and its venue, the Cinema Museum. The Cinema Museum is currently raising money to buy its amazing building and cement its place as the living archive of London&#39;s cinema history. Doors will open at 6.30pm for drinks and snacks amidst the ephemera of cinemas past, showtime at 7.30pm. AccessThere is one step to get into the museum, and a lift to get into the screening hall.Accessible and all gender toilets available.Carers free, service dogs welcome.The film is in Mandarin, Taiwanese and Japanese with English subtitles.No one turned away for lack of funds. Please email us for a discounted or free ticket.If you have any other questions or requests do get in touch. cinemaoftomorrowldn@gmail.com\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_GB\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:locale:alternate\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Programmers of Tomorrow fundraiser screening #1: Goodbye, Dragon Inn (2003) Tickets - London - OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38387/programmers-of-tomorrow-fundraiser-screening-1-goodbye-dragon-inn-2003\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/jpg\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1200\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"584\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/events/adc992ac-7f5e-4973-88cd-484a1e689560.jpg\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Programmers of Tomorrow fundraiser screening #1: Goodbye, Dragon Inn (2003) Tickets - London - OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:url\" content=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38387/programmers-of-tomorrow-fundraiser-screening-1-goodbye-dragon-inn-2003\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:app:name:iphone\" content=\"OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:app:id:iphone\" content=\"722344276\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/events/adc992ac-7f5e-4973-88cd-484a1e689560.jpg?width=1200\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"‘Did you know this theatre is haunted?’The Cinema of Tomorrow (F.K.A PEPCOT) presents the first of three screenings on the theme of ‘Movies at the Movies’. Goodbye, Dragon Inn (2003) is a beautiful, melancholic and quietly funny exploration of intimacy and isolation over the course of the last day at a closing picture palace in Taipei City, Taiwan. Director Tsai Ming-Liang, master of the slow and closely observed, mourns the loss of some of the sacred rituals of cinema going, from cruising to shelling peanuts in the dark.This is the first event (and therefore launch. ) of Programmers of Tomorrow (PoT): A season of workshops and screenings for the future of film exhibition. Consisting of two free workshops, three fundraiser screenings and a film festival all-dayer, PoT will spread knowledge about film programming, build community around the love of movies, and facilitate first timers to put on their first ever public screening.  Read more about it and how to get involved.This screening is a fundraiser for both PoT and its venue, the Cinema Museum. The Cinema Museum is currently raising money to buy its amazing building and cement its place as the living archive of London&#39;s cinema history. Doors will open at 6.30pm for drinks and snacks amidst the ephemera of cinemas past, showtime at 7.30pm. AccessThere is one step to get into the museum, and a lift to get into the screening hall.Accessible and all gender toilets available.Carers free, service dogs welcome.The film is in Mandarin, Taiwanese and Japanese with English subtitles.No one turned away for lack of funds. Please email us for a discounted or free ticket.If you have any other questions or requests do get in touch. cinemaoftomorrowldn@gmail.com\" />\r\n\r\n    <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38387/programmers-of-tomorrow-fundraiser-screening-1-goodbye-dragon-inn-2003\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"OutSavvy | Programmers of Tomorrow fundraiser screening #1: Goodbye, Dragon Inn (2003) | Saturday 5th September 2026 @ The Cinema Museum | £9 to £12 | Find event and ticket information for Cinema of Tomorrow\" />\r\n\r\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n        $(document).ready(function () {\r\n\r\n            var cookieEnabled = navigator.cookieEnabled;\r\n\r\n            // When cookieEnabled flag is present and false then cookies are disabled.\r\n            if (cookieEnabled === false) {\r\n                window.location.replace(\"http://www.outsavvy.com\");\r\n            }\r\n\r\n            // try to set a test cookie if we can't see any cookies and we're using \r\n            // either a browser that doesn't support navigator.cookieEnabled\r\n            // or IE (which always returns true for navigator.cookieEnabled)\r\n            if (!document.cookie && (cookieEnabled === null || /*@cc_on!@*/false)) {\r\n                document.cookie = \"testcookie=1\";\r\n\r\n                if (!document.cookie) {\r\n                    window.location.replace(\"http://www.outsavvy.com\");\r\n                } else {\r\n                    document.cookie = \"testcookie=; expires=\" + new Date(0).toUTCString();\r\n                }\r\n            }\r\n\r\n        });\r\n\r\n        function toggleShowPassword(clientId) {\r\n            let x = document.getElementById(clientId);\r\n            if (x.type === \"password\") {\r\n                x.type = \"text\";\r\n            } else {\r\n                x.type = \"password\";\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        function showShareModal() {\r\n            $('#shareModal').reveal({\r\n                animation: 