            "mimeType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
            "text": "\r\n\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<!--[if lt IE 7]> \t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie6 lte9 lte8 lte7 \">\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 7]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie7 lte9 lte8 lte7 \">\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 8]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie8 lte9 lte8 \">\t\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 9]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie9 lte9 \">\t\t\t\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if (gt IE 9)|!(IE)]><!-->\r\n<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\r\n<!--<![endif]-->\r\n<head id=\"Head1\"><title>\r\n\tProgrammers of Tomorrow fundraiser screening #2: Closed Circuit (1978) Tickets | 03 Oct @ The Cinema Museum, London | £9 to £12 | OutSavvy\r\n</title>\r\n\r\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n        window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];\r\n\r\n        function gtag() { dataLayer.push(arguments); }\r\n\r\n        if (window.location.hash ? window.location.hash == '#cs-scan' : false) {\r\n            gtag(\"consent\", \"default\", { ad_storage: \"granted\", ad_user_data: \"granted\", ad_personalization: \"granted\", analytics_storage: \"granted\", functionality_storage: \"granted\", personalization_storage: \"granted\", security_storage: \"granted\", wait_for_update: 500 });\r\n        }\r\n        else {\r\n            gtag(\"consent\", \"default\", {\r\n                ad_storage: \"denied\",\r\n                ad_user_data: \"denied\",\r\n                ad_personalization: \"denied\",\r\n                analytics_storage: \"denied\",\r\n                functionality_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                personalization_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                security_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                wait_for_update: 500,\r\n            });\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        gtag(\"set\", \"ads_data_redaction\", true);\r\n\r\n        gtag(\"set\", \"developer_id.dZTlmZj\", true);\r\n    </script>\r\n\r\n    <script async src=\"https://consent.studio/outsavvy.com/banner.js\"></script>\r\n\r\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/combres.axd/siteCss/7fe0f610674626944167a99dcfa57a351cfe742a930afe976c016bb3f608223c5956cdd8ab3167f15d9b50a337b27eba0ccb8113b99bd5e19f1cee33041b1821/\"/><script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/combres.axd/siteJs/4ea27d3d3dfdcea6aa2256650964498a5d720acb896b38d1bcbc2a81e57470911dd600418c7f575901cd7b3741c1b3a433126ce5ab0a56f134539cecb5333ade/\"></script>\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"Priority\" content=\"1.0\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"ChangeFrequency\" content=\"daily\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta http-equiv=\"last-modified\" name=\"LastModified\" content=\"2026-08-25\" />\r\n\r\n    \r\n    <meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow\" />\r\n    \r\n\r\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"A matinee showing of a spaghetti western becomes a whodunnit as a member of the audience is shot dead during the gunslinging showdown.The Cinema of Tomorrow (F.K.A. PEPCOT) presents the second of three screenings on the theme of ‘Movies at the Movies’. Closed Circuit (1978) was made for Italian TV, but has since become a beloved cult hit for its mix of murder mystery and a sincere and philosophical love of the ‘magic’ of cinema. Come and watch Closed Circuit as it was never intended, but where it deserves to be, up on the big screen.This event is part of Programmers of Tomorrow (PoT): A season of workshops and screenings for the future of film exhibition. Consisting of two free workshops, three fundraiser screenings and a film festival all-dayer, PoT is spreading knowledge about film programming, building community around the love of movies, and facilitating first timers to put on their first ever public screening.  Read more about it and how to get involved.This screening is a fundraiser for both PoT and its venue, the Cinema Museum. The Cinema Museum is currently raising money to buy its amazing building and cement its place as the living archive of London&#39;s cinema history. Doors will open at 6.30pm for drinks and snacks amidst the ephemera of cinemas past, showtime at 7.30pm. AccessThere is one step to get into the museum, and a lift to get into the screening hall.Accessible and all gender toilets available.Carers free, service dogs welcome.No one turned away for lack of funds. Please email us for a discounted or free ticket.If you have any other questions or requests do get in touch. cinemaoftomorrowldn@gmail.com\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_GB\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:locale:alternate\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Programmers of Tomorrow fundraiser screening #2: Closed Circuit (1978) Tickets - London - OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38388/programmers-of-tomorrow-fundraiser-screening-2-closed-circuit-1978\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/jpg\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1200\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"584\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/events/d5888ac5-0c44-4490-be71-6ce708be88f7.jpg\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Programmers of Tomorrow fundraiser screening #2: Closed Circuit (1978) Tickets - London - OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:url\" content=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38388/programmers-of-tomorrow-fundraiser-screening-2-closed-circuit-1978\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:app:name:iphone\" content=\"OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:app:id:iphone\" content=\"722344276\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/events/d5888ac5-0c44-4490-be71-6ce708be88f7.jpg?width=1200\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"A matinee showing of a spaghetti western becomes a whodunnit as a member of the audience is shot dead during the gunslinging showdown.The Cinema of Tomorrow (F.K.A. PEPCOT) presents the second of three screenings on the theme of ‘Movies at the Movies’. Closed Circuit (1978) was made for Italian TV, but has since become a beloved cult hit for its mix of murder mystery and a sincere and philosophical love of the ‘magic’ of cinema. Come and watch Closed Circuit as it was never intended, but where it deserves to be, up on the big screen.This event is part of Programmers of Tomorrow (PoT): A season of workshops and screenings for the future of film exhibition. Consisting of two free workshops, three fundraiser screenings and a film festival all-dayer, PoT is spreading knowledge about film programming, building community around the love of movies, and facilitating first timers to put on their first ever public screening.  Read more about it and how to get involved.This screening is a fundraiser for both PoT and its venue, the Cinema Museum. The Cinema Museum is currently raising money to buy its amazing building and cement its place as the living archive of London&#39;s cinema history. Doors will open at 6.30pm for drinks and snacks amidst the ephemera of cinemas past, showtime at 7.30pm. AccessThere is one step to get into the museum, and a lift to get into the screening hall.Accessible and all gender toilets available.Carers free, service dogs welcome.No one turned away for lack of funds. Please email us for a discounted or free ticket.If you have any other questions or requests do get in touch. cinemaoftomorrowldn@gmail.com\" />\r\n\r\n    <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38388/programmers-of-