          "content": {
            "mimeType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
            "text": "\r\n\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<!--[if lt IE 7]> \t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie6 lte9 lte8 lte7 \">\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 7]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie7 lte9 lte8 lte7 \">\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 8]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie8 lte9 lte8 \">\t\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 9]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie9 lte9 \">\t\t\t\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if (gt IE 9)|!(IE)]><!-->\r\n<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\r\n<!--<![endif]-->\r\n<head id=\"Head1\"><title>\r\n\tProgrammers of Tomorrow fundraiser screening #3: Night of the Comet (1984) Tickets | 22 Oct @ The Cinema Museum, London | £9 to £12 | OutSavvy\r\n</title>\r\n\r\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n        window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];\r\n\r\n        function gtag() { dataLayer.push(arguments); }\r\n\r\n        if (window.location.hash ? window.location.hash == '#cs-scan' : false) {\r\n            gtag(\"consent\", \"default\", { ad_storage: \"granted\", ad_user_data: \"granted\", ad_personalization: \"granted\", analytics_storage: \"granted\", functionality_storage: \"granted\", personalization_storage: \"granted\", security_storage: \"granted\", wait_for_update: 500 });\r\n        }\r\n        else {\r\n            gtag(\"consent\", \"default\", {\r\n                ad_storage: \"denied\",\r\n                ad_user_data: \"denied\",\r\n                ad_personalization: \"denied\",\r\n                analytics_storage: \"denied\",\r\n                functionality_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                personalization_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                security_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                wait_for_update: 500,\r\n            });\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        gtag(\"set\", \"ads_data_redaction\", true);\r\n\r\n        gtag(\"set\", \"developer_id.dZTlmZj\", true);\r\n    </script>\r\n\r\n    <script async src=\"https://consent.studio/outsavvy.com/banner.js\"></script>\r\n\r\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/combres.axd/siteCss/7fe0f610674626944167a99dcfa57a351cfe742a930afe976c016bb3f608223c5956cdd8ab3167f15d9b50a337b27eba0ccb8113b99bd5e19f1cee33041b1821/\"/><script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/combres.axd/siteJs/4ea27d3d3dfdcea6aa2256650964498a5d720acb896b38d1bcbc2a81e57470911dd600418c7f575901cd7b3741c1b3a433126ce5ab0a56f134539cecb5333ade/\"></script>\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"Priority\" content=\"1.0\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"ChangeFrequency\" content=\"daily\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta http-equiv=\"last-modified\" name=\"LastModified\" content=\"2026-08-31\" />\r\n\r\n    \r\n    <meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow\" />\r\n    \r\n\r\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Where in LA do you wait out the apocalypse? The cinema and the shopping mall of course. The Cinema of Tomorrow (F.K.A PEPCOT) presents the final of three screenings on the theme of ‘Movies at the Movies’. Night of the Comet (1984) is a sci-fi zom-com about sisterhood that whirls ecstaticly across a lusciously depicted and (almost) empty Los Angeles. Our main characters - sisters Regina and Samantha Belmont - were frequently cited by the creators of Buffy the Vampire Slayer. They are the quick-quipping, ass-kicking, fashion-forward blueprints. Roger Ebert and Gene Siskel agreed, throwing a big two thumbs up at this grade-A B-movie. &#128077;&#128077; This event is part of Programmers of Tomorrow (PoT): A season of workshops and screenings for the future of film exhibition. Consisting of two free workshops, three fundraiser screenings and a film festival all-dayer, PoT is spreading knowledge about film programming, building community around the love of movies, and facilitating first timers to put on their first ever public screening.  Read more about it and how to get involved.This screening is a fundraiser for both PoT and its venue, the Cinema Museum. The Cinema Museum is currently raising money to buy its amazing building and cement its place as the living archive of London&#39;s cinema history. Doors will open at 6.30pm for drinks and snacks amidst the ephemera of cinemas past, showtime at 7.30pm. AccessThere is one step to get into the museum, and a lift to get into the screening hall.Accessible and all gender toilets available.Carers free, service dogs welcome.No one turned away for lack of funds. Please email us for a discounted or free ticket.If you have any other questions or requests do get in touch. cinemaoftomorrowldn@gmail.com\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_GB\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:locale:alternate\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Programmers of Tomorrow fundraiser screening #3: Night of the Comet (1984) Tickets - London - OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38389/programmers-of-tomorrow-fundraiser-screening-3-night-of-the-comet-1984\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/jpg\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1200\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"584\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/events/3f2c8065-7633-4de0-b1e9-d7717d68ab22.jpg\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Programmers of Tomorrow fundraiser screening #3: Night of the Comet (1984) Tickets - London - OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:url\" content=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38389/programmers-of-tomorrow-fundraiser-screening-3-night-of-the-comet-1984\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:app:name:iphone\" content=\"OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:app:id:iphone\" content=\"722344276\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/events/3f2c8065-7633-4de0-b1e9-d7717d68ab22.jpg?width=1200\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Where in LA do you wait out the apocalypse? The cinema and the shopping mall of course. The Cinema of Tomorrow (F.K.A PEPCOT) presents the final of three screenings on the theme of ‘Movies at the Movies’. Night of the Comet (1984) is a sci-fi zom-com about sisterhood that whirls ecstaticly across a lusciously depicted and (almost) empty Los Angeles. Our main characters - sisters Regina and Samantha Belmont - were frequently cited by the creators of Buffy the Vampire Slayer. They are the quick-quipping, ass-kicking, fashion-forward blueprints. Roger Ebert and Gene Siskel agreed, throwing a big two thumbs up at this grade-A B-movie. &#128077;&#128077; This event is part of Programmers of Tomorrow (PoT): A season of workshops and screenings for the future of film exhibition. Consisting of two free workshops, three fundraiser screenings and a film festival all-dayer, PoT is spreading knowledge about film programming, building community around the love of movies, and facilitating first timers to put on their first ever public screening.  Read more about it and how to get involved.This screening is a fundraiser for both PoT and its venue, the Cinema Museum. The Cinema Museum is currently raising money to buy its amazing building and cement its place as the living archive of London&#39;s cinema history. Doors will open at 6.30pm for drinks and snacks amidst the ephemera of cinemas past, showtime at 7.30pm. AccessThere is one step to get into the museum, and a lift to get into the screening hall.Accessible and all gender toilets available.Carers free, service dogs welcome.No one turned away for lack of funds. Please email us for a discounted or free ticket.If you have any other questions or requests do get in touch. cinemaoftomorrowldn@gmail.com\" />\r\n\r\n    <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38389/programmers-of-tomorrow-fundraiser-screening-3-night-of-the-comet-1984\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"OutSavvy | Programmers of Tomorrow fundraiser screening #3: Night of the Comet (1984) | Thursday 22nd October 2026 @ The Cinema Museum | £9 to £12 | Find event and ticket information for Cinema of Tomorrow\" />\r\n\r\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n        $(document).ready(function () {\r\n\r\n            var cookieEnabled = navigator.cookieEnabled;\r\n\r\n            // When cookieEnabled flag is present and false then cookies are disabled.\r\n            if (cookieEnabled === false) {\r\n                window.location.replace(\"http://www.outsavvy.com\");\r\n            }\r\n\r\n            // try to set a test cookie if we can't see any cookies and we're using \r\n            // either a browser that doesn't support navigator.cookieEnabled\r\n            // or IE (which always returns true for navigator.cookieEnabled)\r\n            if (!document.cookie && (cookieEnabled === null || /*@cc_on!@*/false)) {\r\n                document.cookie = \"testcookie=1\";\r\n\r\n                if (!document.cookie) {\r\n                    window.location.replace(\"http://www.outsavvy.com\");\r\n                } else {\r\n                    document.cookie = \"testcookie=; expires=\" + new Date(0).toUTCString();\r\n                }\r\n            }\r\n\r\n        });\r\n\r\n        function toggleShowPassword(clientId) {\r\n            let x = document.getElementById(clientId);\r\n            if (x.type === \"password\") {\r\n                x.type = \"text\";\r\n            } else {\r\n                x.type = \"password\";\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        function showShareModal() {\r\n            $('#shareModal').reveal({\r\n                animation: 'fadeAndPop',                   //fade, fadeAndPop, none\r\n                animationspseeed: 300,                       //how fast animtions are\r\n                closeonbackgroundclick: true,              //if you click background will modal close?\r\n                dismissmodalclass: 'close-reveal-modal'    //the class of a button or element that will close an open modal\r\n            });\r\n        }\r\n\r\n    </script>\r\n\r\n<link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"57x57\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-57x57.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"60x60\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-60x60.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"72x72\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-72x72.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"76x76\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-76x76.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"114x114\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-114x114.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"120x120\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-120x120.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"144x144\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-144x144.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"152x152\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-152x152.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"180x180\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-180x180.png\" /><link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"192x192\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/android-icon-192x192.png\" /><link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"32x32\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/favicon-32x32.png\" /><link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"96x96\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/favicon-96x96.png\" /><link rel=\"i