=\"col-lg-10 col-md-10 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 col\">\r\n                    <div class=\"row\">\r\n                        <div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 col\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: flex-end;\">\r\n                            <img src=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/preloader.jpg\" data-src=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/app-notification.jpg\" class=\"app-intro lazy\" />\r\n                        </div>\r\n                        <div class=\"col-lg-8 col-md-8 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 col event-description\">\r\n                            <h3 style=\"text-align: center;\">Track your loved events in your profile or on the OutSavvy App</h3>\r\n                            <ul>\r\n                                <li>Store your tickets securely on the app</li>\r\n                                <li>Browse and buy tickets on the go</li>\r\n                                <li>Get app notifications when tickets go on sale to make sure you are first in the queue</li>\r\n                            </ul>\r\n\r\n                            <div class=\"actions\" style=\"text-align: center; margin-top: 20px;\">\r\n                                <a class=\"btn ui-gradient-green btn-app-store btn-download shadow-lg\" href=\"https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/outsavvy/id722344276\" target=\"_blank\"><span>Available on the</span> <span>App Store</span></a>\r\n                                <a class=\"btn ui-gradient-blue btn-google-play btn-download shadow-lg\" href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.outsavvyapp\" target=\"_blank\"><span>Available on </span><span>Google Play</span></a>\r\n                            </div>\r\n                        </div>\r\n                    </div>\r\n                </div>\r\n                <div class=\"col-lg-1 col-md-1 col-sm-0 col-xs-0 col\"></div>\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div id=\"description\">\r\n            <div style=\"margin-bottom: 0\">\r\n                <section>\r\n\r\n                    <h1 class=\"event-item event-item-name\">Programmers of Tomorrow fundraiser screening #3: Night of the Comet (1984)</h1>\r\n\r\n                    \r\n\r\n                    <div class=\"content-body\">\r\n\r\n                        <div class=\"line-red-holder\">\r\n                            <h4 class=\"line-red\" style=\"margin-top: 5px;\">Details\r\n\r\n                            </h4>\r\n                        </div>\r\n\r\n                        <div class=\"event-description\">\r\n                            <span><p>Where in LA do you wait out the apocalypse? The cinema and the shopping mall of course!</p><p>The Cinema of Tomorrow (F.K.A PEPCOT) presents the final of three screenings on the theme of ‘Movies at the Movies’. <i>Night of the Comet </i>(1984) is a sci-fi zom-com about sisterhood that whirls ecstaticly across a lusciously depicted and (almost) empty Los Angeles. Our main characters - sisters Regina and Samantha Belmont - were frequently cited by the creators of Buffy the Vampire Slayer. They are the quick-quipping, ass-kicking, fashion-forward blueprints. Roger Ebert and Gene Siskel agreed, throwing a big two thumbs up at this grade-A B-movie. 👍👍&nbsp;</p><p>This event is part of Programmers of Tomorrow (PoT): A season of workshops and screenings for the future of film exhibition. Consisting of&nbsp;two free workshops<strong>,</strong> three&nbsp;fundraiser screenings and a&nbsp;film festival all-dayer<strong>, </strong>PoT is spreading knowledge about film programming, building community around the love of movies, and facilitating first timers to put on their first ever public screening! <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://cinemaoftomorrow.substack.com/p/programmers-of-tomorrow-a-season\">Read more about it and how to get involved</a>.</p><p>This screening is a fundraiser for both PoT and its venue, the Cinema Museum. The Cinema Museum is <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.crowdfunder.co.uk/p/the-cinema-museum-buy-our-home\">currently raising money</a> to buy its amazing building and cement its place as the living archive of London's cinema history.&nbsp;</p><p>Doors will open at 6.30pm for drinks and snacks amidst the ephemera of cinemas past, showtime at 7.30pm!</p><p><strong>Access</strong><br>There is one step to get into the museum, and a lift to get into the screening hall.<br>Accessible and all gender toilets available.<br>Carers free, service dogs welcome.<br><br>No one turned away for lack of funds. Please email us for a discounted or free ticket.<br>If you have any other questions or requests do get in touch!<br>cinemaoftomorrowldn@gmail.com</p></span>\r\n                        </div>\r\n\r\n                        \r\n\r\n<div class=\"map-event\">\r\n\r\n    <div id=\"event_map\" class=\"event-map\">\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"map-container\">\r\n\r\n            <div class=\"col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-xs-12\" style=\"padding-right: 0px; padding-left: 0px;\">\r\n                <div class=\"line-red-holder\">\r\n                    <h4 class=\"line-red\">Location\r\n    \r\n                    </h4>\r\n                </div>\r\n                <div class=\"map-padding website-map\">\r\n\r\n                    <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&z=12&query=The+Cinema+Museum%2c+2+Dugard+Way%2c+London%2c+SE11+4TH\" target=\"_blank\" onclick=\"return confirm('Would you like to open Google Maps?');\">\r\n\r\n                        <img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 800 200\"%3E%3C/svg%3E' data-src=\"/Services/MapboxHandler.ashx?lng=-0.1052203&lat=51.49229&w=800&h=200&zoom=16\" class=\"lazy\" alt=\"Event location map\" />\r\n\r\n                    </a>\r\n\r\n                </div>\r\n\r\n                <div class=\"map-padding mobile-map\">\r\n\r\n                    <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?a