                     <div class=\"banner-entry-location\">Royal Vauxhall Tavern - Monday 31st August 2026</div>\r\n                                \r\n                            </div>\r\n                        </article>\r\n                    </a>\r\n                </div>\r\n\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n                </div>\r\n\r\n                <div class=\"menu_footer_buttons\">\r\n                    <div class=\"nav-coll-links\">\r\n\r\n                        \r\n                        <a class=\"nav-coll-link\" href=\"/accountlogin\">Login</a>\r\n                        <a class=\"nav-coll-link\" href=\"/register\">Register</a>\r\n                        \r\n                    </div>\r\n                </div>\r\n\r\n                <footer class=\"menu_footer\">\r\n\r\n                    <div id=\"footer-apps\">\r\n                        <div class=\"actions\">\r\n                            <a class=\"btn ui-gradient-green btn-app-store btn-download shadow-lg\" href=\"https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/outsavvy/id722344276\" target=\"_blank\"><span>Available on the</span> <span>App Store</span></a>\r\n                            <a class=\"btn ui-gradient-blue btn-google-play btn-download shadow-lg\" href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.outsavvyapp\" target=\"_blank\"><span>Available on </span><span>Google Play</span></a>\r\n                        </div>\r\n                    </div>\r\n\r\n                    <div class=\"menu_footer_links\">\r\n                        <a class=\"menu_footer_link\" href=\"/aboutus\">About</a>\r\n                        <a class=\"menu_footer_link\" href=\"/support\">Support</a>\r\n                        <a class=\"menu_footer_link\" href=\"/resell\">ReSell</a>\r\n                        <a class=\"menu_footer_link\" href=\"/contactus\">Contact</a>\r\n                    </div>\r\n                </footer>\r\n\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        \r\n\r\n    \r\n\r\n        <script type=\"application/ld+json\">\r\n        [{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"LiteraryEvent\",\"name\": \"Lost in the Foxglove Presents: In defense of messiness. Visualizer Screening\",\"startDate\": \"2026-09-22T19:00:00+01:00\",\"endDate\": \"2026-09-22T23:00:00+01:00\",\"eventAttendanceMode\": \"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\"url\" : \"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38969/lost-in-the-foxglove-presents-in-defense-of-messiness-visualizer-screening\",\"image\" : \"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/events/6aea47d4-8a9f-4e18-99e4-9a078ded2e3d.jpg\",\"eventStatus\" : \"http://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\"description\" : \"Lost in the Foxglove presents a visualiser screening of second self-published poetry collection: In defense of messiness. Serving as an expansion to IDOM&#39;s literary universe, Bulla filmed and directed her first ever moving picture rendition of the book. The evening will begin with the screening, followed by a 1:1 Q&amp;amp;A with Bulla, chaired by esteemed director and photographer, Kiera Simpson (kierasimpson.com). Afterwards, three London-based creatives positioned across various industries will join the panel and expand the conversation.That&#39;s not all.  There will also be a microbiome kissing booth facilitated by inimitable artist, Emma Walker. Designer and artist, Rose will be selling one of one garments inspired by the poetry collection. And Tooth Gems Cutie will have a variety of tooth gems on offer. Lastly.  Guests will be able to purchase special, second edition signed copies of In defense of messiness. which will include select handwritten (&amp;amp; scanned) poems and a little more insight into the inspiration behind the collection. These can be purchased in advance with your ticket, or in person. \",\"location\": {\"@type\": \"Place\",\"name\": \"Rhizomatic!\",\"address\": { \"@type\" : \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\" : \"Rhizomatic!, 83 Smeed Road\",\"addressLocality\" : \"London\",\"addressRegion\" : \"England\",\"postalCode\" : \"E3 2NR\" },\"geo\" : {\"@type\" : \"GeoCoordinates\", \"latitude\" : \"51.53825\", \"longitude\" : \"-0.0234224\"} },\"offers\": {\"@type\": \"AggregateOffer\", \"availability\":\"http://schema.org/InStock\", \"availabilityEnds\":\"2026-09-22T18:59:00+01:00\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38969/lost-in-the-foxglove-presents-in-defense-of-messiness-visualizer-screening\",\"lowPrice\":22,\"highPrice\":7,\"availabilityStarts\":\"2026-08-23T14:22:35+01:00\",\"validFrom\":\"2026-08-23T14:22:35+01:00\",\"offers\":[{\"availability\":\"http://schema.org/InStock\", \"availabilityEnds\":\"2026-09-22T18:59:00+01:00\",\"name\":\"Low Income\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38969/lost-in-the-foxglove-presents-in-defense-of-messiness-visualizer-screening\",\"price\":7,\"availabilityStarts\":\"2026-08-23T14:22:35+01:00\",\"validFrom\":\"2026-08-23T14:22:35+01:00\",\"@type\":\"Offer\"},{\"availability\":\"http://schema.org/InStock\", \"availabilityEnds\":\"2026-09-22T18:59:00+01:00\",\"name\":\"General Admission\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38969/lost-in-the-foxglove-presents-in-defense-of-messiness-visualizer-screening\",\"price\":10,\"availabilityStarts\":\"2026-08-23T14:22:35+01:00\",\"validFrom\":\"2026-08-23T14:22:35+01:00\",\"@type\":\"Offer\"},{\"availability\":\"http://schema.org/InStock\", \"availabilityEnds\":\"2026-09-22T18:59:00+01:00\",\"name\":\"GA Ticket &amp; *Signed Copy of Poetry Book\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38969/lost-in-the-foxglove-presents-in-defense-of-messiness-visualizer-screening\",\"price\":22,\"availabilityStarts\":\"2026-08-23T14:22:35+01:00\",\"validFrom\":\"2026-08-23T14:22:35+01:00\",\"@type\":\"Offer\"}]},\"organizer\" : { \"@type\" : \"Organization\", \"url\" : \"https://www.outsavvy.com/organiser/lauren-bulla-art\", \"description\" : \"My name is Lauren Bulla. I am a poet, writer, digital &amp;amp; acrylic artist based in North London. I originally moved to England in 2021 to pursue a masters degree in international human rights law.It’s easy for us to bypass hopes of creation as it feels much of it will never lead us anywhere. I want to challenge the voice in my head telling me to stop trying - my events and artworks are a reflection of this effort, that which I hope translates into the lives of my participants.  Much of my work is inspired by life&#39;s larger questions - namely the contradiction and overlapping of &quot;fate versus coincidence&quot;. Though this is often the baseline of many of my works, I also draw inspiration from everyday monsters, queer nightlife, interpersonal relationships, the natural world, and the liminality of our dreams.\", \"name\" : \"Lauren Bulla Art\"}}]\r\n        </script>\r\n\r\n    \r\n\r\n    \r\n\r\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n\r\n        window.addEventListener(\"load\", function () {\n\n            fetch(\"/Default.aspx/GetDoesLove\", {\n                method: \"POST\",\n                headers: {\n                    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n                },\n                body: JSON.stringify({\n                    eventId: 38969,\n                    userId: ''\n                })\n            })\n                .then(r => r.json())\n                .then(data => {\n\n                    const doesLove = data.d;\n\n                    if (doesLove) {\n                        document.body.classList.add(\"is-following\");\n                    }\n\n                });\n\n        });\r\n\r\n        window.addEventListener(\"load\", function () {\n\n            fetch(\"/Default.aspx/GetDoesFollowOrganiser\", {\n                method: \"POST\",\n                headers: {\n                    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n                },\n                body: JSON.stringify({\n                    eventPartnerid: 3279,\n                    userId: ''\n\n                })\n            })\n                .then(r => r.json())\n                .then(data => {\n\n                    const result = data.d;\n\n                    const button = document.querySelector(\".follow-organiser\");\n\n                    if (!button)\n                        return;\n\n                    if (result.CssClass.length > 0)\n                        button.classList.add(result.CssClass);\n\n                    const span = button.querySelector(\"span\");\n\n                    if (span)\n                        span.textContent = result.Text;\n\n                });\n\n        });\n\r\n\r\n        function followorganiser(eventpartnerid) {\r\n\r\n            const button = document.querySelector(\".follow-organiser\");\r\n\r\n            if (button.classList.contains(\"following-button\")) {\r\n                // Send the like to the service\r\n                $.ajax({\r\n                    type: \"POST\",\r\n                    contentType: \"application/json; charset=utf-8\",\r\n                    url: \"/Default.aspx/RemoveFollowOrganiser\",\r\n                    data: '{ userId: \"\", partnerId: \"' + eventpartnerid + '\" }',\r\n                    contentType: \"application/json; charset=utf-8\",\r\n                    dataType: \"json\",\r\n                    success: function (r) {\r\n                        if (r.d != 'undefined' && r.d != '' && r.d != null) {\r\n                            button.classList.remove(\"following-button\");\r\n                            const span = button.querySelector(\"span\");\n                            if (span)\n                                span.textContent = \"Follow\";\r\n                        }\r\n                    },\r\n                    failure: function (r) {\r\n                    },\r\n                    error: function (r) {\r\n                    }\r\n                });\r\n            } el